// src/v4/lens/testgen.dag
//
// Scope: testgen lens — reads substrate declarations and produces TestClaim
//        instances structurally. The producer side of "tests are data, not
//        code" (THESIS facet 3). Output is consumed by lens/coverage.dag
//        which verifies the produced set covers the expected substrate
//        cross-product.
// Anchor: TESTING.md §141 + THESIS §348–368 + §168–182
//
// Owns:
//   - Generator<C> generic carrier (parameterized over substrate concept)
//   - Per-substrate-kind testgen rules. Every rule emits TestClaims whose
//     `kind` is one of std/verification.dag's CLOSED AssertKind
//     (Equals | Diagnostic | Compiles | RoundTrips) — testgen names the
//     AssertKind, it does NOT coin parallel claim vocabulary:
//     - type_construction(
//         (Atom | Conj | Disj | Arrow | Cardinality | Instantiation)
//         — six-connective kernel — OR
//         L1 `Value` **behavior** construction — **unit** `BehaviorValueSubject`
//         arm (only `Behavior::Value`; see subject carriers)
//       ) -> Set<Compiles TestClaim>
//       (kernel + Value-behavior are ONE `type_construction` fold via internal
//       `TypeConstructionSubject` sum — see subject carriers below; not a
//       sixth top-level testgen category)
//     - algebra_law(Algebra × Inhabitant × Law) -> Set<Equals TestClaim>
//     - diagnostic_exhaustiveness(NamedReason variant) -> Set<Diagnostic TestClaim>
//     - lens_applicability(Lens × Program) -> Set<Equals TestClaim>
//     - bidirectional_roundtrip(Language × GrammarProduction) -> Set<RoundTrips TestClaim>
//   - Simulator + boundary conformance (this file, not `lens/simulation.dag`):
//     `simulator_generation(WireContract | Effect | Language) -> Node`;
//     `external_conformance(...) -> Set<{Compiles|Equals|RoundTrips} TestClaim>`.
//     Hermetic generated sim (data, not hand-Rust); `input` = program ∘ sim;
//     live oracle opt-in; AssertKind stays closed-4 (`std/verification.dag`).
//     Contract under-spec ⇒ extend `WireContract` / STOP — not a new kind.
//   - **TestClassification** (Tier × Layer) is a **required field on every
//     `TestClaim`** — canonical home `std/verification.dag` (STRUCTURE.md
//     §248); each fold stamps `classification` consistently with its
//     `Generator<C>.classification` at materialization.
//     - Tier: Tier1 | Tier2 | Tier3 (THESIS correctness tier)
//     - Layer: Unit | Integration | Boundary (TESTING.md test layer)
//   - lens read: () -> Set<TestClaim>
//
// ELSEWHERE (do not duplicate long prose here): C5-1/C5-3 roundtrip contract,
// text-fidelity deferral, TESTING.md §141 ratio targets — see Anchor refs;
// T-18 / `lens/coverage.dag` enforces coverage. Bootstrap contract: TASKS §T-19.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag (substrate to walk)
//   - std/algebra.dag (algebra inhabitance for L7-class testgen)
//   - std/verification.dag (TestClaim output schema)
//   - std/diagnostic.dag (Diagnostic.NamedReason for exhaustiveness testgen)
//   - lens/*.dag (each lens's declared read shape, for applicability testgen)
//   - extdeps/languages/*.dag (bidirectional roundtrip testgen)
//   - extdeps/coordination.dag (WireContract/Effect — simulator-generation arm)
//
// Status: T-19 modeled 2026-05-16 (still-deer-194). **Live:** `import v4.std.verification { TestClassification }` + `type Generator<C>` (M1 compile). **Comment substrate until M2:** subject carriers + `TestgenConcept` + five `fn … -> Set<TestClaim>` folds — loader acceptance per TASKS §T-19.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.
//
// ─── Subject carriers (fold once M2 loads v4 std in one compilation unit) ───
// type TypeConstructionSubject
//   = ConnectiveKernel { connective: Connective }
//   | BehaviorValueSubject
//       // **Unit arm** — L1 `Value` type-construction slice only. Denotes the
//       // same scheduling fact as **`std/node.dag` `Behavior::Value`** (the
//       // unit variant of closed `Behavior`) **without** a `behavior: Behavior`
//       // field that would admit `Transform` / `Branch` / `Loop` / `Bind`
//       (P2 / illegal states unrepresentable). A `t19_manual_anchor_manifest` slug
//       for this arm appears only when a live manual `TestClaim` exists (TASKS §T-19).
//       Scheduling other `Behavior` variants inside `type_construction` = operator STOP +
//       distinct ratified subject arms — not widening this carrier.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4) — **internal** sum under the single
// `type_construction` arm of `TestgenConcept`; classification: 🟢 GREEN.
// Ledger — five patterns on **forward** `TypeConstructionSubject`:
//   1. Fact placement — N/A: both variants schedule through the one
//      `type_construction` fold — not a sixth **top-level** testgen category
//      (TASKS.md T-19: 6th top-level = operator STOP).
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `ConnectiveKernel` carries a `Connective`;
//      `BehaviorValueSubject` is a **unit** arm (no `Behavior` payload) —
//      only the L1 **`Value`** slice is representable here vs six-way
//      connective kernel; structurally distinct shapes.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: not a single richer std/algebra carrier.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one unit picks **one** of kernel vs behavior
//      slice for this category (mutually exclusive).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: behavior slice is not `F<Connective>`
//      nor an enumerated copy of the six-connective set (Practice 7).
//
// type AlgebraLawSubject { algebra: Symbol, inhabitant: Symbol, law: Symbol }
// type DiagnosticExhaustivenessSubject { reason: Symbol }
// type LensApplicabilitySubject { lens: Symbol, program: Node }
// type BidirectionalRoundtripSubject { language: Symbol, production: Symbol }
// type TestgenConcept
//   = TypeConstruction { subject: TypeConstructionSubject }
//   | AlgebraLaw { subject: AlgebraLawSubject }
//   | DiagnosticExhaustiveness { subject: DiagnosticExhaustivenessSubject }
//   | LensApplicability { subject: LensApplicabilitySubject }
//   | BidirectionalRoundtrip { subject: BidirectionalRoundtripSubject }
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// five patterns attempted on the **forward** `TestgenConcept` sum above
// (materializes with the same declaration when M2 loads v4 std in one
// graph — this ledger is binding at that moment, not deferred):
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: lens/testgen.dag (producer) and
//      lens/coverage.dag (T-18 completeness) both dispatch on the
//      category axis; it is the shared testgen-discriminant for the five
//      substrate folds, not a per-consumer scattered fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the five **top-level** arms carry STRUCTURALLY
//      DISTINCT payloads (`TypeConstructionSubject` vs `AlgebraLawSubject`
//      vs …); `TypeConstructionSubject` is itself a documented internal sum
//      (`ConnectiveKernel` | `BehaviorValueSubject` — see above), still
//      ONE arm here. Collapsing to `{ kind: Int, blob: … }` reintroduces
//      illegal states and an open `kind` axis — violates P2 + closed-set
//      discipline. The five-variant top-level sum IS the faithful discriminant.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: a testgen **category** is not an algebra
//      carrier; categories do not trace to a single richer std/algebra.dag
//      construction to dissolve into (algebra-law testgen *reads*
//      algebra, it is not itself an algebra instance).
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one generation unit selects EXACTLY ONE of the
//      five categories — mutually exclusive alternatives (never
//      simultaneous coordinates in a product of independent axes).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the five are not one mechanical
//      `F<X>` / projection over a separately-declared enumerable set X
//      (Practice 7). Payload shapes are heterogeneous per arm; there is
//      no single source set the five enumerate-and-project from.
// Terminal: the irreducible closed partition of T-19 testgen category
// inputs (TASKS.md T-19); a 6th category is a substrate-extension STOP
// (operator ratification), not a silent open enum.
//
// fn type_construction(subject: TypeConstructionSubject) -> Set<TestClaim>
// fn algebra_law(subject: AlgebraLawSubject) -> Set<TestClaim>
// fn diagnostic_exhaustiveness(subject: DiagnosticExhaustivenessSubject) -> Set<TestClaim>
// fn lens_applicability(subject: LensApplicabilitySubject) -> Set<TestClaim>
// fn bidirectional_roundtrip(subject: BidirectionalRoundtripSubject) -> Set<TestClaim>

module v4.lens.testgen

import v4.std.verification { TestClassification }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// PRODUCER LENS. This file owns the GENERIC CARRIER and schedules substrate
// slices. **`src/v4/std/verification.dag`** (`module v4.std.verification`)
// owns the canonical **`TestClaim`** shape **including** `TestgenTier` /
// `TestgenLayer` / `TestClassification` (STRUCTURE.md §248 — Tier×Layer on
// every claim). The five testgen categories map INTO the
// closed four **`v4.std.verification.AssertKind`** variants (`Equals` |
// `Diagnostic` | `Compiles` | `RoundTrips` in **`src/v4/std/verification.dag`**)
// — never a parallel claim vocabulary; manual `assert_kind` Int codes are
// the same four-way projection (not dsl/v3 Assert* / `TestPredicate` surfaces).
//
// `compile_to_dag` today lowers a single module without following
// `import v4.std.*` to on-disk peers (M2 module graph). The subject
// carriers + `TestgenConcept` + rule `fn` signatures therefore remain
// COMMENTED here; they are not deleted — they are the ratified shape to
// materialize when the loader lands. `Generator<C>` below is already
// meaningful with abstract `C` (including `C = TestgenConcept` later).


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Generator<C> — generic carrier: one scheduled generation unit over a
// substrate concept slice `C`. `classification` is the Tier×Layer tag
// copied onto **every** `TestClaim` emitted when this unit lowers to corpus
// data (same `TestClassification` value on each claim — facts-flow-forward).
//
// Coproduct dissolution: Conj record — no ledger.
type Generator<C> {
  classification: TestClassification
  slot: C
}
